# Build context filter.
#
# Both the Containerfile (astral-key) and the Dockerfile (mosaic-identity) do
# `COPY . .`, so everything not listed here is shipped to the daemon as build
# context. A cargo `target/` is multi-GB; sending it turns a ~1 MB build into a
# multi-GB transfer. Measured on the astral-key working clone (2026-10-06) by
# COPYing the context into an image and du-ing it inside the build:
#
#   before: 6112144825 bytes (5.7G)  16864 files
#   after:    808163 bytes (1.0M)      116 files
#
# The 116 files are exactly the clean-clone file set (verified by diffing the
# admitted file list against a fresh `git clone`, which is also 116, zero diff)
# -- so this filter drops build output without eating a build input.
#
# Do NOT add build inputs to this file without checking both builds still work:
#   docker build -f Containerfile .   # astral-key service (what the chart deploys)
#   docker build -f Dockerfile .      # mosaic-identity sidecar

# Cargo build output — the multi-GB reason this file exists.
target/

# Git and GitHub metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.agents/
.claude/
.serena/

# Agent/tooling state that is not a build input.
.skills/
skills-lock.json
HEY.md
AGENTS.md

# Deployment manifests: applied with `kubectl apply`, never compiled in.
casdoor/
charts/
docker/

# Documentation, tests and examples. cargo test fixtures and scratch state.
docs/
tests/
*.md
!README.md

# Nix flake — the dev shell is for humans, the container builds with cargo.
flake.nix
flake.lock
nix/

# Secrets and local overrides. Never belong in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS / backup noise.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej

# Local scratch and worktrees.
scratch/
worktrees/
wt/
